--TEST--
`Core\Router::url`'s two compile errors: a written reference to a method that no `#[Route]` claims, and a `$params` that does not cover the path's captures — `rule:routing/link-target-and-params-are-checked`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// One route with one required capture. The scan that builds the route table
// (`rule:routing/routes-are-compiled-not-registered`) reaches this class
// in the same file, which is all the table needs: `url` asks the whole
// program's table, and where the row was declared is not part of the question.
class Users {
    // `rule:attributes/access-is-a-required-sibling`: without the sibling decision this route is `E0762` and the
    // two link errors below are never reached.
    #[Core\Route(path: "/users/{id}", method: Core\Http\Method::Get)]
    #[Core\Access(allow: Core\Audience::Public)]
    public function show(uint $id): string { return "user " . $id; }

    // No `#[Route]`, so no link can point at it.
    public function format(uint $id): string { return "#" . $id; }
}

// `rule:routing/link-target-and-params-are-checked`'s first refusal: a
// *written* method reference that no `#[Route]` claims.
// The reference is written at the call rather than held in a value, which is the
// whole difference between this error and the throw
// `router-url-and-url-absolute-refuse-the-same-unknown-names.nvst` pins — a
// value reference is not checked here at all, because there is nothing to read.
echo Core\Router::url(Users::format, ["id" => 1]), "\n";

// Its second: a `$params` that does not cover the path's captures. `{id}` is
// required, so its whole segment has nothing to put in it — unlike a `{name?}`,
// whose segment is simply dropped.
echo Core\Router::url(Users::show, []), "\n";

echo "unreachable\n";
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0754]: `Core\Router::url` links to `Users::format`, and that method has no `#[Route]`
   --> case.nvs:23:23
%A
error[E0755]: `Users::show`'s path `/users/{id}` captures `id`, and this `$params` supplies no keys at all
   --> case.nvs:28:6
%A
error: aborting due to 2 errors
To read what a code means and how to fix it, run `nvs agent show <code>`.
